WEBVTT

00:00:14.790 --> 00:00:17.130
Nusumareta kako wo

00:00:17.130 --> 00:00:20.330
Sagashitsuzukete

00:00:21.460 --> 00:00:23.420
Ore wa samayou

00:00:23.420 --> 00:00:27.130
Mishiranu machi wo

00:00:27.330 --> 00:00:32.080
Honou no nioi shimitsuite

00:00:32.330 --> 00:00:33.880
Museru

00:00:34.080 --> 00:00:37.630
Sayonara wa itta hazu da

00:00:37.630 --> 00:00:40.540
Wakareta hazu sa

00:00:40.540 --> 00:00:43.790
Jigoku wo mireba

00:00:44.000 --> 00:00:47.330
Kokoro ga kawaku

00:00:47.460 --> 00:00:52.750
Tatakai wa akita no sa

00:00:54.000 --> 00:00:57.540
Sadame to areba

00:00:57.710 --> 00:01:00.790
Kokoro wo kimeru

00:01:01.040 --> 00:01:05.960
Sottoshite oite kure

00:01:05.960 --> 00:01:07.750
Ashita ni

00:01:07.920 --> 00:01:15.250
Aa tsunagaru kyou gurai

00:01:32.710 --> 00:01:36.750
For a hundred years the Astragius galaxy
had been split by war.

00:01:37.960 --> 00:01:40.960
I was ordered into an operation
whose details were kept from me.

00:01:42.420 --> 00:01:47.130
There, my destiny was changed
the moment I saw her.

00:01:48.960 --> 00:01:52.500
She was apparently the military's greatest secret.

00:01:53.710 --> 00:01:58.170
Since deserting the army, my wanderings
had led me to the city of Uoodo.

00:01:59.500 --> 00:02:02.830
But, for a man like me
who knows only how to fight...

00:02:03.710 --> 00:02:06.420
combat in this city was
something I could not avoid.

00:02:07.710 --> 00:02:11.710
And within the battle, I met her once more.

00:02:13.040 --> 00:02:16.040
She's tied deeply to my destiny.

00:02:16.750 --> 00:02:18.540
But what sort of destiny is it?

00:02:18.880 --> 00:02:23.880
The Deal

00:02:25.790 --> 00:02:28.040
All right! We did it!

00:02:30.080 --> 00:02:33.540
I can't believe we stole
all this jijirium from the cops!

00:02:33.540 --> 00:02:35.330
They must be cryin' in their beers, now!

00:02:35.330 --> 00:02:38.540
Hey, Pops! How much is all this worth?

00:02:39.040 --> 00:02:42.080
Well, let's see. This is only a guess, mind you.

00:02:42.080 --> 00:02:46.420
But I think, it might be worth... Probably, about...

00:02:46.420 --> 00:02:48.460
Oh, it's worth a hell of a lot!

00:02:48.460 --> 00:02:51.630
Oh, wow! A hell of a lot? I can handle that.

00:02:51.630 --> 00:02:54.130
He just doesn't know.

00:02:54.710 --> 00:02:59.380
Coconna, there's enough here to buy
a space cruiser or three!

00:03:00.130 --> 00:03:02.130
What'll I do with all that money?

00:03:06.170 --> 00:03:08.080
Hey, no skimping just 'cuz I'm a girl!

00:03:08.080 --> 00:03:10.540
We divide this four ways even, right?

00:03:10.540 --> 00:03:13.750
Don't worry, we run a democracy here.

00:03:13.750 --> 00:03:16.380
Vanilla, let's have a little toast to dividing it up.

00:03:16.380 --> 00:03:18.250
No reason for us to get down off this high so soon.

00:03:18.250 --> 00:03:20.460
All right! Let's have a real blow out!

00:03:20.750 --> 00:03:24.130
Hey, Chirico! What're you doing?
You should be celebrating with us!

00:03:25.000 --> 00:03:27.290
C'mon, you get a quarter of this, too.

00:03:27.790 --> 00:03:29.290
I don't want it.

00:03:30.750 --> 00:03:33.420
You really take the cake! What's with you?

00:03:33.420 --> 00:03:35.500
You helped out on this, too.

00:03:35.500 --> 00:03:37.920
What'd you go and risk your life for?

00:03:38.500 --> 00:03:40.670
I'm not one of you.

00:03:41.040 --> 00:03:43.000
You three can divide it amongst yourselves.

00:03:43.830 --> 00:03:46.670
Oh, is that so? Well then, don't go
changing your mind later.

00:03:46.670 --> 00:03:50.420
I'll take Chirico's cut,
since I supplied this hideout here.

00:03:50.420 --> 00:03:54.080
The hell you will, Vanilla!
Chirico's cut should go to me!

00:03:54.080 --> 00:03:57.080
What're you talking about?
I was the one who helped him out!

00:03:57.080 --> 00:03:58.670
I should get his cut!

00:03:58.670 --> 00:03:59.880
You greedy little wench!

00:04:00.130 --> 00:04:02.170
I should get the cut.

00:04:02.170 --> 00:04:03.290
Right, Chirico?

00:04:03.290 --> 00:04:06.500
No, it's only right that I get it. Right, Chirico?

00:04:06.500 --> 00:04:09.250
I should get it. Just ask him.

00:04:09.250 --> 00:04:11.080
Don't you think so, Chirico?

00:04:12.330 --> 00:04:13.630
It's mine!

00:04:17.540 --> 00:04:18.710
Chirico!

00:04:18.710 --> 00:04:21.210
You may not want a cut,
but you're as guilty as we are.

00:04:21.210 --> 00:04:22.920
You can't go out now!

00:04:23.540 --> 00:04:25.500
What is with that guy?

00:04:26.330 --> 00:04:27.750
Leave him alone.

00:04:45.330 --> 00:04:50.250
What was it I stumbled across
during that operation?

00:04:51.040 --> 00:04:53.830
I didn't imagine it. She's real.

00:04:54.540 --> 00:04:57.250
The police are trying to kill me.

00:04:58.080 --> 00:04:59.540
But why?

00:04:59.540 --> 00:05:00.830
For what reason?

00:05:01.750 --> 00:05:04.580
That girl is the key to this mystery.

00:05:04.920 --> 00:05:08.710
If I can make contact with her,
I'll be able to learn more.

00:05:18.170 --> 00:05:21.790
Chirico wasn't just trying to steal the jijirium.

00:05:22.540 --> 00:05:26.000
The people he's working for must be here as well.

00:05:26.000 --> 00:05:27.710
But who are they?

00:05:28.460 --> 00:05:31.750
They'll never get out of Uoodo.

00:05:31.750 --> 00:05:34.080
The birds are caged, eh?

00:05:34.580 --> 00:05:37.250
I wouldn't relax just yet, though.

00:05:37.250 --> 00:05:40.500
No matter what, we have to capture him
and force him to talk.

00:05:40.500 --> 00:05:42.960
No matter. It's just a question of time.

00:05:43.790 --> 00:05:46.250
Yes, but just how much time is the question.

00:06:45.000 --> 00:06:47.250
We've gotten a message from headquarters.

00:06:48.000 --> 00:06:51.130
Program One still hasn't left the city.

00:06:51.130 --> 00:06:54.170
The police know it and are still looking for him.

00:06:54.330 --> 00:06:58.330
The cops' mobile patrols
have the city bottled up completely.

00:06:58.330 --> 00:07:00.330
An ant couldn't crawl out of here.

00:07:00.330 --> 00:07:03.380
Sir, the jijirium was stolen by a gang of four.

00:07:03.380 --> 00:07:06.210
Two men, black marketeers. One, a young girl...

00:07:06.210 --> 00:07:09.580
And the last our own Program One: Chirico Cuvie.

00:07:09.920 --> 00:07:12.080
Keep your eyes on the police.

00:07:12.080 --> 00:07:15.040
They'll have to find Chirico eventually.

00:07:15.040 --> 00:07:17.250
Yes, sir. We've already made arrangements.

00:07:18.420 --> 00:07:22.000
If we can find Chirico, we may be able
to find the Prototype as well.

00:07:23.330 --> 00:07:25.710
She has to be somewhere in this city.

00:07:35.630 --> 00:07:37.130
Trouble! Trouble!

00:07:38.000 --> 00:07:39.210
Trouble!

00:07:41.880 --> 00:07:44.420
Chirico! Wake up! It's the cops!

00:07:44.420 --> 00:07:45.420
The cops?

00:07:45.420 --> 00:07:46.420
Come on!

00:07:53.460 --> 00:07:55.960
Come on! Come on! Get up!

00:07:55.960 --> 00:07:58.130
We don't have any time for you to be sleeping!

00:07:58.130 --> 00:08:00.000
Shut up.

00:08:00.000 --> 00:08:01.960
Vanilla, get up!

00:08:03.710 --> 00:08:05.630
We've got trouble!

00:08:07.330 --> 00:08:09.040
Oh, gross!

00:08:09.040 --> 00:08:10.710
Get up, you big, drunk doof!

00:08:10.710 --> 00:08:14.580
Oh, be quiet. We're richer than God now.

00:08:14.580 --> 00:08:17.420
What could we possibly have to worry about?

00:08:17.420 --> 00:08:21.130
We don't have any money yet.
This treasure's useless to us!

00:08:23.290 --> 00:08:25.960
Coconna, what are you talking about?

00:08:26.210 --> 00:08:28.290
We can't leave the city.

00:08:28.290 --> 00:08:31.750
The cops have locked the place up
so tight an ant couldn't get out!

00:08:31.750 --> 00:08:34.420
Son of a...! God dammit!

00:08:35.460 --> 00:08:37.540
I warned you, didn't I?

00:08:37.540 --> 00:08:41.170
My plan said we shoulda
hauled ass outta here yesterday!

00:08:41.170 --> 00:08:44.380
Instead I go and get tanked with this old idiot!

00:08:45.830 --> 00:08:48.170
Why, you little...!
I didn't hear you complaining about it!

00:08:48.170 --> 00:08:50.170
And you drank first!

00:08:50.170 --> 00:08:52.630
I'd say you screwed up your own plan!

00:08:53.210 --> 00:08:55.290
But you talked me into doing it!

00:08:55.290 --> 00:08:56.830
Why'd I ever join up with you?

00:08:56.830 --> 00:09:00.580
Oh, now what? It's your fault we even came here!

00:09:00.580 --> 00:09:03.170
Back off! Where else were we
supposed to go after all that?

00:09:03.170 --> 00:09:04.580
Cut it out!

00:09:04.580 --> 00:09:08.420
While you two are arguing about whose fault it is,
the cops are still looking for us!

00:09:08.420 --> 00:09:10.580
If they find us, we're dead!

00:09:10.580 --> 00:09:12.790
We have to think of a way to get out of here!

00:09:12.790 --> 00:09:16.540
Dammit! All that work for nothing!

00:09:16.540 --> 00:09:17.710
Right, Pops?

00:09:25.250 --> 00:09:27.040
Hey, Chirico.

00:09:27.420 --> 00:09:30.000
Why don't you think of some way
to get out of here?

00:09:30.670 --> 00:09:33.000
You're as guilty as we are.

00:09:33.420 --> 00:09:34.960
Say something!

00:09:39.500 --> 00:09:42.130
Oh, great. He's starting to crack.

00:09:42.130 --> 00:09:44.500
Never shoulda joined up with the old geezer.

00:09:44.500 --> 00:09:47.580
Can you blame him, after losing all that money?

00:09:47.580 --> 00:09:50.630
I'm not senile yet, you idiots.

00:09:50.630 --> 00:09:52.710
I just thought of a way out of this.

00:09:52.710 --> 00:09:55.170
And we don't have to try and escape, either.

00:09:58.500 --> 00:10:01.540
You mean it, Pops? The cops won't find it?

00:10:01.880 --> 00:10:05.670
No, we're gonna sell it to the cops

00:10:05.670 --> 00:10:06.830
What?

00:10:07.210 --> 00:10:09.500
He's definitely gone senile.

00:10:09.500 --> 00:10:12.210
They'd nail us before they'd ever pay. It's nuts!

00:10:12.210 --> 00:10:17.330
No kidding. Quit with the bad jokes
and think of some way to escape.

00:10:17.330 --> 00:10:19.210
Just listen to me.

00:10:19.210 --> 00:10:21.920
The cops want us to panic
and show our hand first.

00:10:21.920 --> 00:10:24.710
That's why they're looking for us so hard.

00:10:24.710 --> 00:10:28.330
It's dangerous!
We don't know what they'll try to do!

00:10:28.330 --> 00:10:31.920
Pops, you're old.
You shouldn't be taking so many chances.

00:10:31.920 --> 00:10:33.580
Thanks for the concern.

00:10:34.580 --> 00:10:36.670
I'm not an ordinary trader, remember?

00:10:36.670 --> 00:10:39.420
I'll set this thing up one way or another.

00:10:39.920 --> 00:10:42.380
I agree with the old man's plan.

00:10:43.170 --> 00:10:45.790
Figures he'd go for the most dangerous one!

00:10:52.250 --> 00:10:56.580
I've ordered a city-wide house-to-house search.

00:10:56.580 --> 00:10:58.540
I've pulled in off-duty officers to search as well.

00:10:58.540 --> 00:11:00.920
You've failed twice already.

00:11:00.920 --> 00:11:03.330
You think the third time will be any different?

00:11:04.380 --> 00:11:07.040
Keep that talk to yourself.

00:11:13.210 --> 00:11:14.460
Chief here.

00:11:14.960 --> 00:11:17.380
Your Excellency! Yes, sir!

00:11:17.880 --> 00:11:19.830
Where's that jijirium?

00:11:19.830 --> 00:11:20.960
What?

00:11:23.210 --> 00:11:25.670
Things are that far out of control?

00:11:25.670 --> 00:11:26.880
No choice then.

00:11:26.880 --> 00:11:28.460
We'll have to use the final option.

00:11:28.710 --> 00:11:31.290
Sir? What final option do you mean?

00:11:31.580 --> 00:11:33.250
Don't you understand?

00:11:33.250 --> 00:11:36.710
This is the perfect opportunity to test it for real.

00:11:36.710 --> 00:11:39.790
Yes, sir! I'll prepare as quickly as possible!

00:11:40.960 --> 00:11:42.880
Sounds like he's angry.

00:11:43.580 --> 00:11:46.630
But I imagine this will be
more effective than your police.

00:12:08.540 --> 00:12:09.420
Captain!

00:12:09.920 --> 00:12:13.790
The old man from the raid
is being taken to the police!

00:12:13.960 --> 00:12:15.540
What? Just him?

00:12:15.540 --> 00:12:16.580
Yes, sir.

00:12:16.580 --> 00:12:19.290
He appeared out of nowhere,
and they arrested him.

00:12:20.960 --> 00:12:24.000
Strange... They must be up to something.

00:12:24.290 --> 00:12:26.330
Perhaps it's Chirico's plan.

00:12:26.330 --> 00:12:28.540
Quit playing dumb and talk!

00:12:29.130 --> 00:12:31.330
Where's the jijirium?

00:12:31.330 --> 00:12:33.290
Where's the rest of your gang?

00:12:35.210 --> 00:12:36.580
Why, you...

00:12:36.580 --> 00:12:38.040
You wanna get it?

00:12:38.040 --> 00:12:39.710
You! Go out into the hall!

00:12:39.710 --> 00:12:41.380
Whoa, don't go nuts, my friend.

00:12:42.040 --> 00:12:46.920
If you kill me, my friends'll sell it
to someone else and leave the city.

00:12:47.290 --> 00:12:51.130
Oh? You people think you can
really get out of the city?

00:12:52.630 --> 00:12:56.540
Snakes can always sniff out a snake hole.
We've got a way out.

00:12:58.960 --> 00:13:00.670
So, what do you say?

00:13:00.670 --> 00:13:02.290
I'm a trader.

00:13:02.290 --> 00:13:04.710
I sell things to people who want them.

00:13:04.710 --> 00:13:08.880
You want to sell it to us?
You're pissin' me off, Pops!

00:13:08.880 --> 00:13:10.710
You won't get a better bargain.

00:13:10.710 --> 00:13:14.920
Hey, if you don't want it my partners will
sell it someplace else and leave.

00:13:15.210 --> 00:13:17.710
You're at our mercy, and you...

00:13:18.210 --> 00:13:21.750
What are you gonna do? Buy it or not?

00:13:21.750 --> 00:13:23.330
We'll buy it, Gotho.

00:13:27.330 --> 00:13:30.750
Chief, we're gonna buy back
what they stole from us?

00:13:30.750 --> 00:13:33.250
I like a man who can make
a quick decision, Chief.

00:13:33.250 --> 00:13:37.290
Okay, one more thing.
The price is three billion gildans.

00:13:37.750 --> 00:13:40.330
Very well. We'll get the money together.

00:13:40.330 --> 00:13:44.420
In gold, please. Paper money just won't do.

00:13:44.830 --> 00:13:49.880
I hear you. Be at the
bombed-out coliseum in three hours.

00:13:49.880 --> 00:13:52.420
All right, the deal's done.

00:13:52.420 --> 00:13:55.170
Gotho, we're on the level about this, right?

00:13:56.040 --> 00:13:57.790
I'll be leaving now.

00:13:57.790 --> 00:14:00.380
I think I can see myself out.

00:14:01.710 --> 00:14:05.130
I hope the main man shows.

00:14:05.130 --> 00:14:08.000
He'll show. He has to.

00:14:08.000 --> 00:14:10.500
She's as vital to him as she is to us.

00:14:10.670 --> 00:14:12.500
The deal's made!

00:14:12.500 --> 00:14:15.170
They'll be paying three billion gildans! In gold!

00:14:15.170 --> 00:14:16.500
No way!
All right!

00:14:16.500 --> 00:14:18.630
The master trader strikes again!

00:14:18.630 --> 00:14:21.580
Hey, this hasn't worked out yet, Pops!

00:14:21.580 --> 00:14:24.420
The cops are bound to try and double-cross us.

00:14:24.420 --> 00:14:25.830
They followed me.

00:14:27.920 --> 00:14:32.290
They had a car tailing me up until I lost them
in a funeral procession near the crematorium.

00:14:32.290 --> 00:14:33.330
Great.

00:14:33.670 --> 00:14:35.580
They're pulling something already.

00:14:35.580 --> 00:14:37.750
Probably practicing for when they do it for real!

00:14:37.750 --> 00:14:40.830
Listen, pal. You think I'd die
when there's money on the line?

00:14:40.830 --> 00:14:43.580
Relax, a cat couldn't have
followed me back here.

00:14:43.580 --> 00:14:44.710
I'm going with you.

00:14:45.460 --> 00:14:47.500
Chirico, it's too risky. Don't!

00:14:47.500 --> 00:14:50.170
Right. The cops'll kill you!

00:14:50.170 --> 00:14:52.040
No, I have to go.

00:14:53.170 --> 00:14:55.880
I thought you didn't want a cut.

00:14:55.880 --> 00:15:00.330
I still don't, but I want to be
his bodyguard for this.

00:15:08.830 --> 00:15:11.580
I've got a present for you boys!

00:15:11.580 --> 00:15:12.630
Later!

00:15:12.630 --> 00:15:15.080
Hey, that's the jijirium truck!

00:15:15.080 --> 00:15:16.170
What?

00:15:16.170 --> 00:15:18.460
Hey! You there! Stop!

00:15:18.830 --> 00:15:19.830
Damn!

00:15:22.580 --> 00:15:23.880
Meow...

00:15:51.920 --> 00:15:55.540
Chief Iskui! It's me, Gotho!

00:15:55.790 --> 00:15:57.500
I'm here for the exchange.

00:15:57.500 --> 00:16:00.670
It's time. Now show yourself!

00:16:06.880 --> 00:16:10.000
This'll be the first time someone ever
made a monkey out of me...

00:16:18.960 --> 00:16:22.000
Iskui, where are you? Show yourself!

00:16:29.540 --> 00:16:32.040
You've got guts to come alone, Gotho.

00:16:32.040 --> 00:16:35.880
I've kept my end of the bargain, Chief.

00:16:35.880 --> 00:16:37.580
You gonna pay me?

00:16:44.920 --> 00:16:46.540
Where's the jijirium?

00:16:46.540 --> 00:16:49.460
On its way back to your headquarters, I imagine.

00:16:54.460 --> 00:16:55.790
You're sure?

00:16:56.750 --> 00:16:57.670
Roger.

00:16:58.960 --> 00:17:03.040
Chief, a young girl was reported
to have abandoned a tanker truck.

00:17:03.040 --> 00:17:06.040
We've confirmed the jijirium is inside.

00:17:07.540 --> 00:17:10.750
Now then, do I get my gold?

00:17:24.630 --> 00:17:26.080
I'll take that.

00:17:27.000 --> 00:17:29.670
I'd take a look around you, first.

00:17:41.960 --> 00:17:45.710
Thought you'd pull something like this, Chief.

00:17:46.920 --> 00:17:48.710
Shall I press this button, Chief?

00:17:48.710 --> 00:17:51.040
You probably won't be able to see it from here,

00:17:51.040 --> 00:17:53.750
but when the truck blows
it'll take police headquarters with it!

00:17:55.500 --> 00:17:58.710
Now then, I'll take my money.

00:18:02.330 --> 00:18:05.960
You, there! There's a bomb in the tanker.

00:18:07.080 --> 00:18:08.790
Have it disarmed.

00:18:08.790 --> 00:18:09.580
Yes, sir!

00:18:09.580 --> 00:18:13.210
You think I won't press this?
Don't underestimate me!

00:18:13.670 --> 00:18:17.880
Go ahead and push it. I could really care less.

00:18:17.880 --> 00:18:20.670
We can always build a new
headquarters for ourselves.

00:18:20.670 --> 00:18:21.420
What?

00:18:21.420 --> 00:18:24.540
But the second you do,
we'll fill you full of holes!

00:18:26.380 --> 00:18:30.210
If you want to live, I suggest you get lost.

00:18:43.790 --> 00:18:45.540
Chirico! Vanilla! Let 'em have it!

00:18:46.040 --> 00:18:46.960
Let's go!

00:18:50.420 --> 00:18:51.330
There he is!

00:18:51.330 --> 00:18:52.420
Return fire!

00:18:52.710 --> 00:18:53.880
Over there!

00:19:14.040 --> 00:19:15.210
There it is!

00:19:15.210 --> 00:19:17.420
We don't need the truck
now that we have the gold!

00:19:19.710 --> 00:19:21.210
Let's move it, Vanilla!

00:19:21.210 --> 00:19:23.460
Gotcha. Okay! Let's go.

00:19:31.420 --> 00:19:33.630
Chirico, we have the money! Let's go!

00:19:44.130 --> 00:19:45.880
C'mon, Chirico! Move it!

00:19:45.880 --> 00:19:47.330
What's he doing?

00:19:56.040 --> 00:19:58.750
You know, don't you, Chief?

00:19:58.750 --> 00:20:00.960
Why are you trying to kill me?

00:20:02.250 --> 00:20:03.250
Why?

00:20:03.710 --> 00:20:05.710
Tell me the reason!

00:20:17.170 --> 00:20:19.750
Uh-oh, something weird just showed up.

00:20:27.880 --> 00:20:30.920
If we stay here, we're dead for sure!

00:20:31.080 --> 00:20:32.920
Chirico! We're getting out of here!

00:20:32.920 --> 00:20:34.670
Get away as fast as you can!

00:22:11.170 --> 00:22:12.880
You're deadly...

00:22:12.880 --> 00:22:14.420
Who are you?

00:22:17.630 --> 00:22:21.960
Near-perfect reflexes,
almost supernatural intuition...

00:22:25.630 --> 00:22:28.000
Who... are you...?

00:22:54.170 --> 00:22:55.580
Next Episode

00:22:56.130 --> 00:23:00.210
Last night, all was lost
and soaked in the acid rain.

00:23:00.330 --> 00:23:04.830
Today, they pursue the means
to buy all their lives' dreams.

00:23:04.960 --> 00:23:08.630
Tomorrow morning,
weak faith and petty consciences

00:23:08.630 --> 00:23:10.630
will cover the ruined city with gold.

00:23:11.000 --> 00:23:14.880
Uoodo, a Pandora's Box
created by the Hundred Years War.

00:23:14.880 --> 00:23:17.380
True intentions are finally brought to light.

00:23:17.580 --> 00:23:19.330
Next time, "Rescue"

00:23:19.330 --> 00:23:24.130
Rescue

00:23:19.330 --> 00:23:24.130
Next Time

00:23:19.580 --> 00:23:21.080
And the day after tomorrow?

00:23:21.080 --> 00:23:22.920
That no one can predict.

00:23:42.380 --> 00:23:45.880
Samishii toki mo

00:23:45.880 --> 00:23:49.420
Kanashii toki mo

00:23:49.420 --> 00:23:55.790
Itsumo anata ga me ni ukabu

00:23:56.250 --> 00:23:59.790
Hitori no toki mo

00:23:59.790 --> 00:24:03.250
Aitai toki mo

00:24:03.250 --> 00:24:09.500
Itsumo anata wa mune no naka

00:24:09.500 --> 00:24:13.000
Tooku hanarete itemo

00:24:13.000 --> 00:24:16.380
Tatoe wakarete itemo

00:24:16.580 --> 00:24:22.920
Kono yo no hikari to tomo ni mabushiku

00:24:23.290 --> 00:24:29.250
Ano hi no anata ga...
